reviews.text:
So where do I start with this review? Wishing to remain as balanced and as fair as possible, overall our stay was “just about okay” but there really were some serious downsides with this hotel.

Let me start with the positives:
-	The hotel is in a great location for the skiing;
-	Rooms are spacious and clean;
-	The hotel is very attractive and really well appointed; and 
-	The pool areas is pleasant. 

What about the rest:
-	Check in is really slow and we were in our rooms for c1hr before the bags arrived - well they didn't really arrive we grabbed them off a trolley sitting on another floor;
-               The service is, and was, shocking. From the get go it was slow, required repeated chase ups and at some points we just gave up on items arriving. This was for breakfast, lunch and dinner;
-	Don’t think I’ve even been in an hotel where the managers stated “we knew that your group would be difficult to please and we would never meet your expectations”. Not really how to win your guests’ confidence or hope; 
-	Dinner – strangely the main restaurant was “being renovated” or was “fully booked due to an event” so they were pushing all customers to the buffet. We saw neither renovations nor an event – and made worse by the fact that it was open for lunch. They did open the restaurant when pushed – but it took some pushing. When it did the food was really very good. Can only surmise that it was either too much hassle to open the restaurant or not as cost effective. The stories didn’t add up;
-	Little or no advice when it came to skiing equipment – which for a ski resort was short of amazing;
-	Don't think that we got the room that we booked. Suspect, as some other customers were kicking off at the same time we arrived, that they did some juggling with the rooms;
-               Buffet – very ordinary and pretty standard, nothing special but given there is nowhere else you are trapped;
-	Transport – given the location of Gulmarg you would have thought that (a) the hotel would be well versed on getting customers to and from the resort and (b) they would have either lots of vehicles or at least good contingency. They had neither. We booked a number of cars to take us back to the airport in plenty of time – we should have told them we were leaving the day before so they could arrange on time. Sparing the details – they were late, some never arrived, there were lots of hotel cars in the car park but were not used. In short - almost missed our flights and caused significant stress for the whole group.  Given this should be the bread and butter for an hotel like this – it was very disorganized and a shambles. No amount of excuses, like there is a traffic jam or they are broken down, washed with some seasons Delhi-ites. 
-                  Corridors – we were on a few lower floors and they smelt very damp and slightly of sewage.

Points to note:
- Make sure you get your own car and driver – do not rely on the hotel;
- Bring alcohol, if you want, as the hotel is dry;
- if you do rely on the hotel transport make sure that you (a) leave lots of buffer time and (b) chase, chase and chase for confirmation; and 
- Gulmarg isn't for beginners.
